# Review Gate

Before finalizing any change to blog content, run a short review pass and report high-signal findings first.

## Review Priorities

+ **Correctness first:** flag inaccurate commands, unsafe defaults, broken flows, or advice that can mislead readers.
+ **Risk language:** for risky Git operations (`rebase`, `amend`, force push, branch deletion), ensure guardrails and caveats are explicit.
+ **Context realism:** avoid absolute wording when team workflows differ; prefer scoped phrasing ("usually", "in my workflow", "often").
+ **Actionability:** every finding includes a concrete wording change or command-level fix.
+ **Style alignment:** keep first-person voice, concise explanations, and `+` bullet style used in this repo.

## Minimum Checkpoints

+ Confirm command snippets are safe to run as written.
+ Confirm branch-sensitive commands include the intended branch context when relevant.
+ Confirm cleanup commands mention squash/rebase edge cases when needed.
+ Confirm final feedback is ordered by severity, then optional polish notes.

## Review Output Shape

+ Start with findings (highest severity first).
+ Include file path references for each finding.
+ If no issues are found, state that explicitly and note any residual testing or workflow assumptions.
